TITLE:: REVisualsTape
summary:: What a piece sends to HomewareVisuals, with the time of each message
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/RCVisuals, Classes/REOfflineTap, Classes/RERenderedPlayer

DESCRIPTION::
The messages link::Classes/RCVisuals:: sends (notes, births, cycles, lines, the score feed...) with the second of each, in the format HomewareVisuals' code::scripts/viz-record.mjs:: records from the bridge: code::[[seconds, "/address", arg, ...], ...]::, plain JSON, one entry per line, Symbols as strings (the pages read plain strings). A render records one through RCVisuals' sink with the offline clock's seconds (link::#*record::), shifts it to the take's start, the WAV's timeline (link::#-shifted::), and writes it next to the render as code::<take>.viz.json:: (HomewareSC's code::scripts/take.sh render --viz::; the state taps' frames are merged in by its Python side, link::Classes/REOfflineTap::). A rendered take played live (link::Classes/RERenderedPlayer::) plays the tape back through RCVisuals (link::#-play::), and a page plays one alone with code::?replay=<url>::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: record
A new tape recording: the sink installed (the previous one kept, put back by link::#-finish::), every message with code::timeFunc.value:: as its time.
argument:: timeFunc
The seconds of a message (the calling thread's seconds by default; a render gives its offline clock's).

METHOD:: read
The file read back: the times and the numeric arguments as numbers, the rest as strings. Nil when the file is missing or is not a tape.
argument:: path

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: record
METHOD:: finish
The previous sink back.
METHOD:: isRecording

METHOD:: add
argument:: secs
argument:: path
argument:: args
METHOD:: addEntries
Entries from elsewhere (the state taps' frames), added and sorted in.
METHOD:: sort
METHOD:: entries
METHOD:: size
METHOD:: isEmpty
METHOD:: duration
The last entry's seconds.
METHOD:: countBy
Address → count.
METHOD:: shifted
A new tape with every time minus code::secs::, clamped at 0.
argument:: secs

METHOD:: write
argument:: path
returns:: The path.

METHOD:: play
A Routine from code::atSecs:: on the clock, each entry sent at code::atSecs:: plus its seconds through code::RCVisuals.sendArgs::, or to code::func.(path, args)::.
argument:: atSecs
The clock's seconds (now when nil): on SystemClock, the logical seconds a take's player starts at.
argument:: clock
SystemClock; an link::Classes/REOfflineClock:: in a test.
argument:: func
returns:: The Routine.
METHOD:: stop
METHOD:: isPlaying

EXAMPLES::

code::
// a render (scripts/sc/take_render.scd)
t = REVisualsTape.record({ clock.seconds });
... clock.advanceTo(endBeat) ...
t.finish;
t.shifted(startSecs).write(out.drop(-4) ++ ".viz.json");

// a page preview without sound: HomewareVisuals' public/recordings/<name>.json, then
// http://localhost:5173/Personal_SC/.../HadronLake3_LSystemViz_w0_260929.html?replay=/recordings/<name>.json

// played back live by hand (RERenderedPlayer does this with the WAV)
t = REVisualsTape.read(path);
t.play(thisThread.seconds + 1);
t.stop;
::
